                {
                    "id": "commentary",
                    "classList": [
                        "commentary"
                    ],
                    "heading": "Commentary",
                    "text": [
                        "The most significant change this month was organizing most data attached to an object into a mostly reusable struct and passing this struct into a function. It's probably overkill but it ended up saving a lot of time. The struct isn't that big anyway. I'm not actually sure what I'm worried about. This caused a cascade of errors due to references to a lot of variables no longer existing but nothing really related to logic so it was a lot of simple fixes."
                    ]
                },
